</code></pre> <p><code>usecols</code> is the cheapest optimisation of all: never load columns you do not need.</p> <p>pandas and Arrow</p> <p>pandas 2.x can store columns as Apache Arrow arrays (<code>dtype_backend="pyarrow"</code> in readers). pandas 3.0 makes an Arrow-backed string type the default. Arrow strings are compact and fast, and moving data to Polars, DuckDB or Spark becomes almost free (Chapter 3).</p>

